  ('a0b53151-989c-4176-b3fd-0c9469f8800f','127 Archery in Albertville, Alabama is organized as a volunteer club with an ASA affiliation, putting it inside the same 3D archery and bowhunting circuit that a lot of Southern clubs use to structure their shooting calendar. Being ASA-affiliated generally signals a group oriented around realistic animal targets and scored rounds rather than pure target archery, which tends to draw a bowhunting-minded crowd in this corner of Alabama. Lindsey Goodwin is listed as a contact for the club, a useful starting point for anyone who wants specifics on shoot dates, course conditions, or how to get involved, since the club''s day-to-day details aren''t posted publicly beyond that.'),
  ('b6667471-a85e-437a-93e9-1266fd11f260','Listed in the IBO pro shop directory under a phone number rather than a business name, this Monterey, Virginia archery shop serves the rural Highland County area from deep in the Allegheny Mountains. An IBO listing points to ties with International Bowhunting Organization competition and 3D shooting circles, which tend to matter more in mountain counties like this one where bowhunting is a major part of local outdoor life. Beyond the IBO directory entry, there''s no additional detail on hours, inventory, or services published for this shop. Given the unusual listing format, anyone trying to reach it is better off calling the number directly than expecting a storefront with a sign matching it.'),
  ('f4a67cb4-0ee8-4dc9-bbf2-4d3a7f1d4c8c','Another entry pulled from the IBO pro shop directory, this Mishawaka, Indiana business appears under a phone number instead of a storefront name, serving archers in the South Bend metro area of northern Indiana. Its IBO listing ties it to the International Bowhunting Organization''s competitive 3D scene, a popular circuit in this part of the Midwest where bowhunting season draws serious interest each fall. No further public detail exists on hours, product lines, or services offered at this location beyond the directory entry itself. Given the listing format, the most reliable way to get real information, whether it''s inventory, bow tuning, or directions, is to call the number directly.'),
  ('49338e2f-112c-4496-a62a-c707b67d4a17','The Abilene Bowhunters Association, based just outside Abilene in Buffalo Gap, Texas, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club that runs a 3D course for members to practice on lifelike animal targets. That combination, ASA competition ties plus an actual 3D range, points to a club built around bowhunters who want to sharpen their shot before deer season rather than casual target shooters. West Texas has a strong hunting culture, and a club like this one likely fills a real community role for local archers. Jon Earley is listed as a contact for the association, a good first call for questions on shoot schedules, course access, or how to become a member.'),
  ('15aba05a-9cd6-4e60-884f-54b375eb382d','Aim Takers Archery, based in London, Kentucky, in the state''s southeastern hill country, is a volunteer club with ASA affiliation, tying it into a broader 3D archery and bowhunting competition circuit rather than functioning as a purely casual shooting group. That part of Kentucky has deep bowhunting roots, and an ASA-affiliated club gives local archers a structured way to compete and practice on realistic targets ahead of hunting season. Candace Metcalf is listed as the club''s contact, a useful starting point for questions on membership, shoot schedules, or course conditions since detailed public information about day-to-day operations isn''t otherwise available. Reaching out directly remains the most reliable way to get current specifics.'),
  ('4153a98e-78ac-4397-8c1e-5e09a0b1fb20','Alaskian Bowhunters Association, listed under Wasilla, Alaska, appears in the IBO pro shop directory despite its association-style name, suggesting a business or group tied into the International Bowhunting Organization''s competitive circuit in the Matanuska-Susitna Valley north of Anchorage. Alaska''s hunting season and short shooting window before winter make organized bowhunting groups a meaningful part of the local outdoor community, and an IBO connection points to 3D-style competition shooting rather than purely recreational range time. Beyond the IBO directory listing, no further detail on hours, services, or membership is available. Anyone curious whether this is a shop, a club, or both should contact them directly, since the name and the directory category don''t fully line up on paper.'),
  ('9f1b0df2-e646-498c-abf8-901b344910a2','Allen Archery, located in the small town of Allen, Oklahoma, is a volunteer club with ASA affiliation, placing it within the same 3D archery and bowhunting competition network used by clubs across much of the South and Midwest. Rural Oklahoma has a strong hunting tradition, and an ASA-affiliated club in a town this size likely functions as a central gathering point for local archers rather than one option among many. Jake Linker is listed as the contact for the club, the logical first call for anyone with questions about shoot dates, course conditions, or how membership works, since detailed day-to-day operations aren''t published beyond that contact information.'),
  ('bd2a91ea-f89f-4deb-925a-5ec5ac1f8a0a','Allied Sportsmen, based in Alden, New York just east of Buffalo, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club running a 3D course alongside a lesson program and 15 lanes for members to use. That''s a fuller lineup than many clubs offer, combining structured instruction for newcomers with realistic 3D targets for bowhunters sharpening their aim before deer season in western New York. Fifteen lanes is a meaningful amount of shooting capacity for a club setup, suggesting group shoots and events are a regular part of how Allied Sportsmen operates. John Floriano is listed as the club''s contact for anyone with questions about joining, current shoot schedules, or course access, since further specifics aren''t posted publicly beyond that.'),
  ('6fb86a2a-9ca7-4372-a46f-5c8479158c18','American Outdoors Company, based in Covington, Louisiana on the north shore of Lake Pontchartrain, operates as a volunteer club with ASA affiliation, connecting it to the wider 3D archery and bowhunting competition scene active across the Gulf South. Despite the company-style name, its classification as a volunteer club suggests a member-driven group rather than a retail business. Louisiana''s long hunting season keeps bowhunting a year-round interest for many members in clubs like this, and ASA ties typically mean scored 3D rounds are part of the regular calendar. Ronnie Alpha is listed as the contact for anyone interested in shoot dates, membership, or course conditions, since further operational detail isn''t published beyond that.'),
  ('d7375d5e-f530-4b1e-b69e-dbf05c518c34','Anderson County Sportsmans Club, in Lawrenceburg, Kentucky in the Bluegrass region, is a volunteer club with ASA affiliation, tying its archery program into the broader 3D competition and bowhunting circuit that many Kentucky clubs participate in. As with many sportsmen''s clubs, archery is likely one part of a broader set of outdoor activities the club supports, though the ASA tie specifically points to organized 3D shooting rounds. Central Kentucky has a strong hunting tradition, and a club like this one often plays a community role beyond just providing a place to shoot. Gary Baugh is listed as the contact for anyone with questions about membership, shoot dates, or course access, since further detail isn''t published publicly beyond that.'),
  ('c898aa43-03f5-47a4-892e-2c3a660823ca','Androscoggin Valley Fish and Game, in Milan, New Hampshire, shows up in the IBO directory with a 3D archery course on the property, putting it on the radar of anyone chasing IBO-style 3D shoots in the North Country. That IBO listing also references a pro shop connected to the club, though specifics on inventory or services aren''t confirmed. Fish-and-game clubs like this one often blend archery with hunting, fishing, and conservation work, so the range is usually one part of a bigger outdoor operation rather than a dedicated archery business. Anyone planning a visit should contact the club ahead of time to confirm 3D course access, shoot schedules, and whether the pro shop is open to non-members.'),
  ('ff46a64d-b0e5-4747-92f7-23fd62df93af','Ani Kawi Bowhunters is a volunteer-run 3D archery club affiliated with the ASA, based in Lawrenceburg, Tennessee. That ASA tie means the club follows the association''s format for 3D target shoots, which tends to draw bowhunters looking to sharpen their range estimation before hunting season starts. As with most volunteer clubs, the course and schedule are kept up by members rather than paid staff, so shoot dates can shift and aren''t always posted somewhere official. There''s no indication of a pro shop, lessons, or a separate field course here, just the 3D format the ASA affiliation implies. Anyone interested in shooting with this club should reach out directly to confirm current dates and whether visitors are welcome.'),
  ('2079d363-812b-4762-b7da-c2ff27eda5ed','Apache Bowhunters is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club operating out of Lockbourne, Ohio, just south of Columbus. The ASA tie means the club runs its course to that association''s 3D format, aimed at bowhunters wanting realistic range-estimation practice before hunting season. Being volunteer-run, the shoot schedule and course upkeep depend on members rather than paid staff, which usually means shoot dates travel by word of mouth more than through a public website. There''s no listed pro shop, lesson program, or separate field course, just the 3D shooting the ASA affiliation implies. Contact Apache Bowhunters directly to find out about upcoming shoots and whether guests can join in.'),
  ('170ecbc5-4a14-4856-a714-4f7fba53cc36','Appalachian Archers runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D club out of Marion, North Carolina, in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains. The ASA affiliation points to a course built for bowhunters and 3D competitors working on judging distance against realistic foam targets rather than flat range faces. Since it''s volunteer-run, shoot days and course upkeep depend on the membership, and schedule details tend to travel through the club''s own network more than a public calendar. Nothing here confirms a pro shop, lessons, or a field course at this location, just the 3D format tied to the ASA listing. Anyone wanting to shoot an ASA-style course near Marion should get in touch with Appalachian Archers directly for current dates.'),
  ('f89428b7-e81e-4330-954f-fefc241c4d3c','Appalachian Bowhunters Association, based in Buckhannon, West Virginia, appears in the IBO directory with a pro shop noted alongside the listing. That IBO tie suggests the group caters to bowhunters and 3D shooters following the IBO''s competitive format, even though nothing here confirms a 3D course, lessons, or a range yardage on-site. West Virginia''s mountainous terrain makes it prime bowhunting country, and organizations with names like this typically grow out of that local hunting culture rather than starting life as a retail operation. Details on the pro shop''s inventory, hours, or whether the range is open to the public aren''t available here, so reaching out to Appalachian Bowhunters Association directly is the way to get a straight answer before visiting.'),
  ('ce90d8c3-1ff7-46bb-9816-79bb4b807c97','Appomattox River Archery, LLC runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Church Road, Virginia, a small rural community named for its spot along the Appomattox River. The ASA affiliation points toward a course laid out for bowhunters and competitive 3D shooters rather than a flat indoor range, and being volunteer-run means the shoot calendar is set and maintained by the membership itself. There''s no confirmed pro shop, lesson program, or separate field course tied to this listing, so what''s here is the 3D format the ASA connection implies and little else. Anyone interested in shooting an ASA-style 3D course along the Appomattox River should contact the club directly for current shoot dates and guest policy.'),
  ('3b74d924-c436-41e1-82a3-9ff15171ca8f','Archers For Christ is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Paris, Texas, and the name signals a faith-based community built around the shooting. The ASA tie means the course follows that association''s realistic 3D format, which tends to appeal to bowhunters and competitive 3D shooters working on distance judgment. As with most volunteer clubs, day-to-day operations and scheduling come from the membership rather than paid staff, so news of upcoming shoots is likely to travel through the club''s own network. There''s no confirmed pro shop, lesson program, or field course tied to this listing, just the 3D format the ASA affiliation implies. Reach out to Archers For Christ directly for shoot dates and visitor policy.'),
  ('6893669b-b2b7-436e-abd7-537b19943a5d','Archers Haven LLC, in Newport, Vermont, shows up in the IBO directory with a pro shop noted for the location, placing it within Vermont''s Northeast Kingdom, a rural region known for hunting and outdoor recreation. The IBO connection suggests ties to bowhunting and 3D-style competitive archery, though nothing here confirms an actual 3D course, lessons, or range yardage on-site. As an LLC rather than a club, Archers Haven likely operates as a small commercial business, but specifics on hours, inventory, or public range access aren''t captured in this listing. Anyone near Newport interested in the pro shop or shooting options should contact Archers Haven LLC directly, since the directory listing confirms affiliation without spelling out day-to-day details.'),
  ('98850897-1be2-4ff2-b9e0-4a78595df23a','Archery Connection, listed in Middleburgh, New York, appears in the IBO directory alongside a noted pro shop, tying it to the bowhunting and 3D archery world the IBO represents. Middleburgh sits in a rural, Catskills-adjacent part of upstate New York with a strong hunting tradition, which fits the kind of clientele an IBO-listed pro shop would typically serve. This listing doesn''t confirm a 3D course, lessons, or range yardage at the location itself, just the IBO tie and pro shop reference. Anyone interested in gear, IBO-related information, or shooting options at Archery Connection should contact the business directly, since the directory listing confirms affiliation without spelling out day-to-day services or hours.'),
  ('9922bec9-5cf8-40f1-b153-95a47a490306','Archery Paradise is a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Iowa City, Iowa, home to the University of Iowa. The ASA affiliation points to a course built for realistic 3D target shooting, the format bowhunters often use to practice judging distance before hunting season. As a volunteer club, the shoot calendar and course upkeep depend on its members rather than paid staff, so current dates are more likely to circulate through the club''s own network than a public listing. There''s no confirmed pro shop, lesson program, or field course here, just the 3D format the ASA connection implies. Anyone in the Iowa City area interested in ASA-style 3D shooting should contact Archery Paradise for schedule and guest information.'),
  ('6aef00a1-52de-45cf-b5b7-fdb1e3d57a63','Arizona Bowhunters Association, listed in Casa Grande, Arizona, appears in the IBO directory as a pro shop, tying it to the International Bowhunting Organization''s network of affiliated retailers and ranges rather than USA Archery''s target-archery circuit. That IBO connection suggests a bowhunting-oriented focus, fitting for a name built around bowhunters rather than Olympic-style shooters. Beyond the IBO pro shop listing, current records don''t confirm a 3D course, field course, or formal lesson program at this location. Hunters and 3D shooters in the Casa Grande area who want gear, tuning, or setup help tied to bowhunting equipment should contact Arizona Bowhunters Association directly to confirm what''s in stock and available.'),
  ('67146bf5-92a3-40c8-9569-e398ea77f784','Arizona Junior Olympic Archery Development, known as AZJOAD, is a USA Archery affiliated club in Phoenix running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program for young shooters and an Adult Archery Program for grown-up beginners and returning archers. That dual-track structure makes it a natural fit for families where kids and parents both want to learn recurve or compound fundamentals under the same club umbrella. As a hybrid facility, it likely blends structured club programming with some open access, though specific amenities like a pro shop or 3D course aren''t confirmed. Phoenix-area families interested in JOAD or adult coaching should reach out to AZJOAD directly for enrollment details and schedules.'),
  ('8458804e-c8ed-41a7-a1ed-7ad6f438c25f','Arrow Dynamic Archery, a USA Archery affiliated hybrid facility in Harbor City, part of the Los Angeles Harbor area, runs both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, and confirms lessons as part of its offering. That combination points to a club built around structured coaching for shooters of every age, from kids working toward JOAD milestones to adults picking up a recurve bow for the first time. As a hybrid operation it likely mixes club programming with some open shooting access, though a pro shop or 3D course isn''t confirmed. South Bay archers interested in JOAD or adult lessons should contact Arrow Dynamic Archery directly for current class availability.'),
  ('3d6079e3-a85c-4943-9979-eda2199cc396','Arrowhead Archery Academy in Carlton, Minnesota, stands out for the breadth of its USA Archery affiliated programming: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, Field Archery, and Olympic Archery in the Schools all run under one roof. That range of offerings, spanning youth development, adult participation, school partnerships, and multiple shooting formats, makes it one of the more fully built-out clubs in northeastern Minnesota. As a hybrid facility it likely combines this structured programming with additional open access for members. Families or schools in the Carlton and Duluth-area region interested in any of these programs should contact Arrowhead Archery Academy directly for enrollment and scheduling information.'),
  ('9fcff797-0707-4cf8-b605-6b589ddfdade','Arrows for Christ Ministries/WWCC is a faith-based archery club in Waxahachie, Texas that has carried ASA affiliation, tying it to the 3D bowhunting-style format the Archery Shooters Association organizes nationally. Records show that affiliation status listed as expired in 2025, so archers shouldn''t assume current ASA-sanctioned events or standing without checking first. The ministry framing suggests archery is used here as a vehicle for community and faith alongside the sport itself, distinct from a purely competitive club. No pro shop, 3D course, field course, or lessons are separately confirmed. Anyone in the Waxahachie area interested in this group should contact them directly to confirm current status and activities.'),
  ('af81d804-4348-4cb2-8832-f0c061c8ce87','Arrowstotle Archery, a USA Archery affiliated club in Plano, part of the Dallas-Fort Worth suburbs, runs a Junior Olympic Archery Development program alongside an Adult Archery Program, giving both kids and grown-ups a structured path into recurve and compound shooting. The clever name aside, its hybrid classification suggests club programming paired with at least some open shooting access for members. A pro shop, 3D course, or field course isn''t confirmed as part of what''s offered here, so those interested in gear or alternative formats should ask directly. Plano-area families weighing JOAD or adult lessons should reach out to Arrowstotle Archery to check current enrollment and schedule details.'),
  ('2b317b47-c120-496e-8ad2-0574f4c2bd28','Arts Archers is a USA Archery affiliated hybrid club in Fullerton, Orange County, running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for young shooters. Unlike some clubs on this list, no separate adult program is confirmed here, suggesting the club''s structured offering may currently center on youth development rather than grown-up beginners, though informal adult participation could still exist outside JOAD specifically. No pro shop, 3D course, or field course is documented either. Orange County families interested in getting a child started in Olympic-style recurve shooting through JOAD should contact Arts Archers directly to ask about age requirements, equipment needs, and current openings in the program.'),
  ('e0a34f6b-939a-46a3-9478-a56968b567c9','Ascension Archery, on the East Bay side of the Bay Area in San Leandro, is a USA Archery affiliated hybrid club offering both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. That combination means a single club serving an entire family, whether that''s a child working through JOAD levels or a parent starting from zero as an adult beginner. No pro shop, 3D course, or field course is confirmed as part of its setup, so the focus here appears to be structured target-archery instruction rather than a full-service retail range. San Leandro and East Bay archers interested in either program should reach out to Ascension Archery directly for schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('286bafe2-73be-4e99-bbd3-5c1ba30a8ae6','Ascent Archery in Greeley, on Colorado''s northern Front Range, is a USA Archery affiliated hybrid club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program. As with several JOAD-only clubs, no separate adult program, pro shop, 3D course, or field course is documented, which points toward a club primarily built around developing young archers through USA Archery''s youth pathway rather than offering a broader set of services. That focus can be a real advantage for families specifically looking for structured, coach-led youth instruction rather than a general-purpose range. Greeley-area parents interested in JOAD for their kids should contact Ascent Archery directly to ask about age groups, cost, and current program openings.'),
  ('bdb52e19-eabb-4e0e-ab76-3834f60a4949','Asheville Archery Training Center, in the mountains of western North Carolina, is a USA Archery affiliated hybrid club combining a Junior Olympic Archery Development program with an Adult Archery Program and confirmed lessons, making it one of the more instruction-forward clubs in the region. That trio of confirmed offerings, youth development, adult programming, and direct coaching, suggests a facility genuinely built around teaching archers of any age and starting point rather than just providing lanes. No pro shop or 3D course is confirmed alongside that. Asheville-area residents interested in learning to shoot or getting their kids into JOAD should reach out to the Training Center directly for class schedules.'),
  ('7ea657aa-838f-4ab4-b474-61d8a93bffca','Aslan Archery, in the Denver suburb of Highlands Ranch, is a USA Archery affiliated hybrid club with an unusually full program slate: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and Field Archery all run under one club. That range covers both the structured youth-to-adult target pathway and the more varied, terrain-based 3D and field formats that hunters and recreational shooters often gravitate toward. As a hybrid facility it likely pairs this programming with some open access for members, though a pro shop isn''t separately confirmed. Douglas County archers interested in any of these programs should contact Aslan Archery directly for current schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('01c3d3b0-30ed-427b-a639-c7e6d08419cc','Atlanta Archery Club is based in Dunwoody, one of the northern suburbs inside metro Atlanta''s perimeter, and as a USA Archery affiliated hybrid facility it runs a genuinely broad program: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and confirmed lessons. That mix serves everyone from a kid entering JOAD to an adult wanting hands-on coaching to a hunter interested in 3D-format practice, making it one of the more complete club offerings in the metro area. No pro shop is confirmed alongside these programs. Atlanta-area families and adult beginners interested in any of these tracks should contact Atlanta Archery Club directly for enrollment details and current schedules.'),
  ('9850f9a2-8c78-4f11-8bf2-726860047c01','Average Joes JOAD builds its program around USA Archery''s structured pathway from a base in Coon Rapids, part of the Twin Cities metro. Kids come up through Junior Olympic Archery Development''s coached, level-based curriculum, while the club''s companion Adult Archery Program keeps grown beginners and returning shooters progressing on the same national standard rather than treating them as an afterthought. That two-track setup means a family doesn''t have to split a kid and a parent across separate organizations to both get real instruction. Twin Cities archers looking for structured, USA Archery-certified coaching rather than an open walk-in range should contact Average Joes JOAD directly for current session times, age groups, and enrollment steps.'),
  ('4503935f-5550-467a-b299-97be9c499e16','High desert archers in Victorville have a genuinely full-spectrum option in AVGC Archery, a USA Archery affiliated club running three programs at once. Kids enter through Junior Olympic Archery Development, adults get their own structured Adult Archery Program, and shooters wanting to sharpen distance judgment can step into the club''s 3D archery offering. That breadth of programming under one affiliation is uncommon for a club this size and means a JOAD kid and a 3D-shooting parent could plausibly train through the very same organization. Southern California high desert families and adult beginners alike should contact AVGC Archery directly to confirm current schedules, which locations host each program, and how to enroll.'),
  ('7931d02b-6fa8-4926-9db8-b62c3fee62b2','Avon Bowmen Inc operates a volunteer-run 3D archery club out of Avon, in western New York''s Genesee Valley, under an Archery Shooters Association affiliation. Volunteer clubs like this one exist because members build and maintain the course themselves, so what''s on the ground reflects however much time the group puts into upkeep rather than a corporate budget. That usually produces close-knit shoots where regulars know the terrain and help newcomers learn the ropes rather than leaving them to guess yardages alone. Anyone in the Avon or greater Rochester area interested in 3D-format shooting, judging distance on foam targets across natural terrain, should reach out to the club directly for membership details and upcoming shoot dates.'),
  ('87a3a049-57fa-4d62-91c5-3e0bd4446fb8','Axis Archery LLC pairs two things you don''t always find together: an ASA-affiliated 3D archery course and an on-site pro shop, based in Paige, Texas, east of Austin. The 3D affiliation means members shoot foam-animal targets judged on realistic yardage, exactly the kind of practice bowhunters lean on heavily ahead of deer season, while the attached shop gives shooters a place to handle gear, restring a bow, or grab supplies without a separate trip into town. Registered as an LLC rather than a bare volunteer group, the setup suggests more organization behind the scenes than a typical backyard club. Central Texas archers and bowhunters should contact Axis Archery directly for course access, shop hours, and membership terms.'),
  ('53cc3a7c-a981-42d0-887c-3567165f1a86','A USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program runs out of B.K-Archery JOAD Club in Bristow, Virginia, giving Prince William County families a structured on-ramp for young shooters. JOAD clubs follow USA Archery''s national curriculum, meaning kids move through defined skill levels under certified coaching instead of picking up form unsupervised, which matters to parents who''d rather their child learn correctly the first time. The club''s name makes its focus plain: this is a junior-pathway program first, not a general walk-in range. Families in Bristow and the greater Northern Virginia region interested in enrolling a young archer should contact the club directly for session times, age requirements, and equipment needs.'),
  ('db1e247b-c932-434b-81be-810b7b14b7fd','B&W Easy Pull LLC shows up in the International Bowhunting Organization''s directory of ranges, operating as a commercial archery facility in Attic, Ohio. An IBO listing usually signals a course built with 3D-style bowhunting practice in mind, since IBO is one of the sport''s main sanctioning bodies for that format, though the specifics of B&W''s own layout, hours, and pricing aren''t confirmed here. Ohio bowhunters prepping for IBO-sanctioned shoots, or anyone wanting realistic yardage practice ahead of deer season, have reason to give this one a call. Reach out to B&W Easy Pull directly to confirm current course details, walk-in access, and whether day-use or membership pricing applies.'),
  ('12243a32-0ccc-471d-9f29-0b663215beb9','Back 2 the Wild Archers runs both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program under one USA Archery affiliation in Centerville, along Utah''s Wasatch Front. That two-track structure lets a family bring a kid into structured JOAD coaching while a parent or older sibling works through the adult curriculum with the very same club, instead of splitting across two separate organizations. Wasatch Front archers wanting national-standard USA Archery instruction, rather than an informal walk-in range, have a home base here. As with most affiliate clubs, practice locations and times follow the club''s own calendar, so reach out directly to confirm current sessions, age requirements, and how to get started.'),
  ('5c3c6ec7-d93d-47fd-b929-388735cb18f2','One of two clubs sharing the name Backwoods Bowhunters in this data set is based in Pipestem, West Virginia, near Pipestem Resort State Park in the state''s southern mountains. This club has carried an Archery Shooters Association affiliation in the past, though current records show that status lapsed as of 2025, so it isn''t presented here as an active certification, prospective members should confirm directly whether ASA-sanctioned shoots are still running. Southern West Virginia''s mountainous terrain and strong bowhunting tradition make it a natural fit for a 3D-style club regardless of sanctioning status. Anyone in the Pipestem area interested in the club should contact it directly to confirm current activity and whether the ASA affiliation has been renewed.'),
  ('9d16dc5b-f21e-4d34-ba1b-756eff2a5cde','The second Backwoods Bowhunters in this data set operates well outside West Virginia, a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in El Reno, just west of Oklahoma City. The ASA affiliation points to a foam-target course judged on distance estimation, the standard format for 3D competition and bowhunting practice, maintained here through member labor rather than paid staff. That volunteer model usually means the course and shoot schedule reflect however much time the membership puts in, so newcomers should expect a close-knit group rather than a commercial walk-in setup. Central Oklahoma archers and bowhunters interested in 3D practice should contact the El Reno club directly for membership details and upcoming shoot dates.'),
  ('17af6b6b-e726-4e54-aab3-3910f2b6ac28','Backwoods Sportsmen runs as a volunteer-based, ASA-affiliated 3D archery club out of El Dorado Springs, in southwest Missouri not far from the Kansas line. The ASA affiliation means the course is built for foam-target 3D shooting, the discipline most bowhunters use to sharpen distance judgment before deer season, and the volunteer structure means the range exists because members show up and maintain it themselves rather than because a company runs it for profit. That setup tends to reward regulars who put in the work with a course that keeps evolving year over year. Southwest Missouri archers interested in 3D shooting should reach out to Backwoods Sportsmen directly to ask about membership and the current shoot schedule.'),
  ('affee3ed-c18a-4334-a0a0-685a5266262a','Backyard Archers JOAD runs its USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program out of Linn, a small Osage County town roughly between Jefferson City and Columbia. The club''s name suggests informal, grassroots origins, but the JOAD affiliation means young shooters here follow USA Archery''s structured national curriculum with certified coaching rather than picking up form on their own. For a rural stretch of mid-Missouri without many nearby options, having a certified JOAD program gives local families a legitimate path into competitive target archery. Parents interested in enrolling a young archer should contact Backyard Archers JOAD directly to confirm current session times, age minimums, and what equipment kids need to start.'),
  ('e46cdaa8-b867-4020-8919-2abe11273ae1','Weber County''s Ogden hosts BAKCOU JOAD Club and its USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program, one of several JOAD-certified clubs along northern Utah''s population corridor. The JOAD affiliation means young shooters here follow USA Archery''s national curriculum with certified coaching rather than an informal drop-in setup, complete with defined age groups and skill levels rather than an ad hoc program run purely on volunteer instinct. That structure gives Ogden-area families a genuine, trackable path for kids getting into target archery. Parents interested in enrolling a child should contact BAKCOU JOAD Club directly to confirm current practice times, age requirements, and registration steps before showing up.'),
  ('8f471dbb-aa53-4c87-9f2f-556531d585c8','Bates Farm 3D Archery Range delivers exactly what its name promises: a volunteer-run, ASA-affiliated 3D course set on farmland in Decatur, in Alabama''s Tennessee Valley, with six lanes and lessons available for shooters wanting real coaching before tackling the foam-target course. The ASA affiliation and confirmed 3D layout make this a solid stop for bowhunters sharpening distance judgment ahead of season, while the lesson option means newcomers aren''t left to figure out form on their own. North Alabama''s active bowhunting culture fits well with a farm-based course like this one. Anyone interested in shooting at Bates Farm should contact the range directly to confirm current lesson scheduling, course access, and membership terms.'),
  ('0171fb11-2e70-491b-96e6-d313d4cfe117','Bay Path Archers Inc. runs both a USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program and 3D archery offerings out of Southbridge, in south-central Massachusetts'' Worcester County. That pairing means young shooters can start in JOAD''s structured, competition-focused curriculum and later branch into 3D''s foam-target, distance-judging format, or members can pursue both formats depending on interest. South-central Massachusetts doesn''t have an overwhelming number of USA Archery affiliates, so a club running both JOAD and 3D programming gives local families real range without traveling far. Parents or adult shooters interested in either program should contact Bay Path Archers directly to confirm current session times and how to enroll.'),
  ('627277f6-c231-42b4-9465-2a94770ce079','Bayou Bowmen Archery Club, a volunteer-run 3D archery group affiliated with the Archery Shooters Association, operates out of New Iberia, in the heart of Cajun Country along the Bayou Teche. The ASA affiliation points to a foam-target course built for distance-judging practice, the format most Louisiana bowhunters use to prep for the state''s long deer season across swamp and farmland terrain. Being volunteer-run means the course and shoot schedule reflect whatever time the membership puts into upkeep, so newcomers should expect a club that runs on its own community rather than paid staff. Acadiana-area archers and bowhunters interested in 3D shooting should reach out to Bayou Bowmen directly for membership details and shoot dates.'),
