  ('0d625a1b-4258-4e74-be39-f3cb3dae6e3a','Bear Creek Xtreme runs as a hybrid facility in Englewood, Colorado, and its USA Archery affiliation anchors it around the Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) pathway. That program structure means the club is set up to bring young archers up through recurve and compound fundamentals with an eye toward regional and national competition, rather than just offering open range time. For families in the south Denver area looking for structured youth coaching, a JOAD-affiliated club is one of the more reliable signals that real instruction is happening on-site. Reach out to Bear Creek Xtreme directly for current JOAD session schedules and enrollment.'),
