  ('a8ba15b6-0afe-4522-b68e-8282304fb96a','BOPA, Inc. in Troy, Michigan appears in the International Bowhunting Organization''s own pro shop directory, placing it among Michigan''s IBO-recognized bow retailers rather than a standalone public range. That listing typically points to a business focused on bow sales, tuning, and accessories for bowhunters, though the specifics of any in-store shooting lanes aren''t detailed here. Archers in the Detroit metro area with IBO ties, or anyone shopping for hunting archery gear, should contact BOPA directly to confirm what services and shooting space, if any, are currently available on-site before making the trip to Troy.'),
  ('ae93799e-2e3b-4b97-ad4f-1b5b950f5a9f','Bow Bending Believers of CBA in Medina, New York is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club serving bowhunters in this part of western New York, not far from the Niagara region. Merle Fredericks is the listed contact for the club, continuing the pattern of grassroots ASA clubs run by a single dedicated volunteer rather than paid staff. The club''s name suggests ties to a broader CBA organization, though specifics on that connection aren''t detailed here. Archers interested in 3D-style practice or membership should reach out directly to Bow Bending Believers to find current shoot dates, since informal scheduling is typical for clubs of this size.'),
  ('7b246a79-4699-44df-befe-9c1fa865dd46','The Bowhunters Club in Maryville, Tennessee is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club near Knoxville that stands out among 3D clubs in this area for offering both a pro shop and lessons alongside its course, a combination that gives beginners a real path into the sport rather than just a place for experienced shooters to practice. Jeff Ledbetter serves as the club''s current contact, typical of the volunteer leadership structure common to ASA-affiliated clubs. That mix of instruction, equipment support, and a competitive 3D format makes it a solid option for East Tennessee archers at any level, though confirming lesson availability directly is still recommended.'),
  ('cd5dca0b-fb0a-4701-8e8b-7d5d48bd6735','BowTown in Blanchard, Oklahoma is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club serving bowhunters just south of Oklahoma City, with Carl Shipley currently listed as the point of contact for membership and shoot-day questions. Like most ASA clubs of this size, it runs on volunteer effort rather than paid staff, so schedules tend to flex around member availability instead of posted hours. The club gives central Oklahoma archers a home course for practicing the unmarked-distance, foam-target shooting that ASA''s 3D format is built around. Anyone interested in visiting or joining should reach out to Carl directly rather than assuming drop-in access is available.'),
  ('bc9ba838-efd4-4313-9a48-b60740b78790','Box Butte Archery in Hemingford, Nebraska is a USA Archery affiliated club in the Nebraska Panhandle that runs a Junior Olympic Archery Development program alongside 3D archery, giving young shooters a structured path into competitive target archery while also serving the area''s bowhunting-minded archers. That JOAD-plus-3D combination is a useful fit for a rural community where a single club often has to serve a broad range of ages and interests rather than specializing narrowly. Families and archers in the Panhandle region interested in youth coaching or 3D practice should contact Box Butte directly for current class schedules and course access.'),
  ('a4fb65a5-5ecd-40af-9697-24c025fec396','Boyle County Fish & Game Club in Stanford, Kentucky pairs its ASA-affiliated 3D archery course with the broader fish-and-game club model common across central Kentucky, where a single organization often covers archery alongside other outdoor pursuits. Billy Henson is the current contact for the club, and as with most ASA-affiliated groups, membership and shoot-day access run through that volunteer point of contact rather than posted business hours. The 3D course gives area bowhunters realistic practice ahead of deer season, and archers new to the Stanford area should reach out to Billy directly to learn about joining or visiting the range.'),
  ('a32bae43-151e-474d-a21e-e318b06ba5f0','Brazos County Archery Club in Bryan, Texas runs an ASA-affiliated 3D course serving the Bryan-College Station area, home to Texas A&M and a sizable population of students and locals interested in bowhunting and target archery alike. Tracey Sadler currently serves as the club''s contact, and as with other ASA-affiliated volunteer clubs, reaching out directly is the way to learn about shoot days and membership rather than expecting posted hours. The 3D format gives Brazos Valley archers realistic practice for bowhunting season, and the club is a solid option for anyone in the College Station area looking for a competitive-style course.'),
  ('6215cbd6-23b5-4aef-8bba-a8c0c154f6d4','Brighton Archery - SELCRA in Brighton, Michigan is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, giving the club a genuine cross-generational reach rather than serving just kids or just adults. The SELCRA name points to a tie with a broader local recreation association, which often means access to shared facilities beyond what a standalone archery club could offer on its own. Families in the Brighton and greater Livingston County area looking for structured, USA Archery-aligned coaching for either juniors or adults should contact the club directly for current class schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('f0c93adb-825a-45fb-8828-be3d30aa144a','Broken Arrow 3-D Course in Charleston, Illinois runs under ASA affiliation, putting it on the national 3D archery circuit rather than operating as a standalone backyard range. That affiliation matters for bowhunters: ASA courses are built around lifelike foam targets set at unmarked or marked yardages, the same skill set that translates directly to field shooting. Central Illinois has a strong bowhunting tradition, and a club like this gives local archers a place to sharpen range estimation and shot placement before deer season rather than only shooting flat paper. Course details, target counts, and shoot schedules aren''t listed here, so anyone wanting to shoot a round or ask about joining should contact the club to confirm current dates and access.'),
  ('5280b8b4-5b66-4bfc-9f37-8e7d22913fee','In Bowling Green, Kentucky, Broken Arrow Archery carries ASA affiliation, which places it among the clubs hosting or shooting sanctioned 3D archery rounds rather than just informal target practice. For archers in south-central Kentucky, that means a course built to test judgment on realistic animal targets at varying, often unmarked distances, a format popular with bowhunters tuning up before whitetail season. The listing doesn''t include specifics on target counts, course length, or public shoot dates, so treat this as a starting point rather than a full picture. Anyone interested in shooting a round, joining as a member, or volunteering to help run the course should reach out to the club directly for current details.'),
  ('3e5abb63-411a-4f78-9c52-02d734455396','Jasper, Indiana is home to a Broken Arrow Archery Club chapter that holds ASA affiliation, meaning it''s set up to run 3D archery in the sanctioned format bowhunters use to train for judging distance and shot angle on realistic targets. Southern Indiana has plenty of whitetail habitat, and clubs like this tend to draw members looking to stay sharp between hunting seasons as much as competitive 3D shooters chasing points. This entry doesn''t list course details, shoot schedules, or membership costs, so what''s here is a starting point rather than the full story. Interested archers should get in touch with the club to find out about current shoot dates, guest policy, and how to join.'),
  ('4563993d-bf7d-49d5-a10f-4533d5f80c27','There''s a Broken Arrow Archery Club in Elkin, North Carolina, part of the ASA-affiliated 3D circuit that draws serious bowhunters from across the Yadkin Valley region. ASA affiliation means the course is designed around foam animal targets at realistic, sometimes unmarked ranges, a format that rewards the same skills used chasing deer in the Piedmont''s hardwood terrain rather than flat-range paper shooting. No details on target counts, course length, or public shoot calendar are available in this listing. Anyone in the Elkin area wanting to shoot a round, check on membership, or find out when the course is open to visitors should reach out to the club directly rather than assume it''s a walk-up range.'),
  ('5e20e8d7-ff4d-46b4-9312-98a4d3079dfe','Henderson, Minnesota, a small river town along the Minnesota River, has its own Broken Arrow Archery Club running under ASA affiliation. That puts the club''s course in the sanctioned 3D format, built around foam animal targets rather than paper bullseyes, which is exactly the kind of practice southern Minnesota bowhunters use to prepare for deer season judgment calls on range and angle. The listing here doesn''t include course length, target counts, or a public shoot schedule, so treat it as a lead rather than confirmed details. If you''re an archer near Henderson looking to shoot a 3D round or join, contacting the club directly is the way to get current, accurate information.')
) AS v(id, description)
WHERE r.id = v.id::uuid AND r.is_claimed = false;
